================================================================================
 SU3HOB-ladder
 Harmonic-oscillator (Talmi-Moshinsky) transformation brackets in the SU(3)
 basis, with the SU(3) > SO(3) isofactors generated from the U(2) pseudo-spin
 ladder operators.
================================================================================

WHAT IT COMPUTES

  The general Talmi-Moshinsky bracket

      <e1 l1, e2 l2 : L | T(d) | e1' l1', e2' l2' : L>

  for an arbitrary mass-ratio parameter d, via the SU(3)-basis expression of

      R.K. Kalinauskas, A. Stepsys, D. Germanas, S. Mickevicius,
      "Calculation of harmonic oscillator brackets in SU(3) basis",
      Nucl. Phys. A 1056 (2025) 123033;  arXiv:2501.19131.

  The bracket reduces to one sum over Wigner d-functions of the
  reflection-containing Talmi-Moshinsky matrix, weighted by products of
  SU(3) > SO(3) isofactors of the chain U(6) > U(3) x U(2).


HOW THE ISOFACTORS ARE OBTAINED  (what distinguishes this package)

  Not from any SU(3) coupling library.  The U(2) factor of the chain is
  generated by the pseudo-spin bilinears

      J+ = a+(1).a(2),   J- = J+^T,   Jz = (N1 - N2)/2,

  and J+ is an SO(3) scalar, so it acts within fixed (E,L) and raises
  M = (e1-e2)/2 by one.  Because the U(3) and U(2) labels inside [E] of U(6)
  are complementary, classifying this pseudo-spin at fixed (E,L) IS the
  SU(3) > SO(3) classification.  Hence:

      highest weights  =  ker J+  in the block M = J
      the rest         =  obtained by lowering with J-

  The kernel comes from the Gram matrix G = J-J+ = J^2 - M(M+1), whose exact
  eigenvalues are J'(J'+1) - M(M+1), so the rank decision is never marginal.
  Lowering (rather than solving each M separately) is what fixes ONE
  consistent multiplicity label alpha across the whole tower.

  Consequences: the isofactors come out orthonormal by construction; there is
  no K-matrix, no inverse square root of an overlap matrix, and no outer
  multiplicity to resolve.  The package is fully self-contained.

  The full derivation is given in the accompanying article (see ACCOMPANYING
  ARTICLE below), which sets out the construction step by step.


BUILD AND TEST

    make            builds test_hob_su3 and hob
    make check      runs the validation driver, compares with the reference
    make bench      builds the timing / accuracy drivers in bench/
    make clean

  Only a Fortran 2008 compiler is required for the library and the CLI.
  BLAS/LAPACK is needed for bench/ only (dsyev and matmul).


PUBLIC INTERFACE  (module hob_su3)

    call hob_init(Emax)                        ! once, before anything else
    call hob_build_basis(E, L, b)              ! coupled basis of the block
    call hob_prepare(E, L, S)                  ! d-INDEPENDENT isofactor towers
    call hob_eval(S, d, H)                     ! whole HOB matrix for this d
    val = hob_bracket(S, e1,l1,e2,l2, e1p,l1p,e2p,l2p, d)
    i   = hob_state_index(b, e1, l1, l2)
    a0  = alpha_mult(E, twoJ, L)               ! Racah inner multiplicity

  The design point: hob_prepare does not depend on d.  Prepare a block once,
  then evaluate it for as many mass ratios as wanted -- "prepare once,
  evaluate many".


VALIDATION

  test_hob_su3 checks, for every (E,L) up to Emax and several d:
    (i)   alpha_0 against the Racah inner-multiplicity formula, per tower;
    (ii)  orthonormality, max |HOB.HOB^T - I|;
    (iii) the involution property, max |HOB^2 - I|;
    (iv)  element-by-element agreement with the classical Talmi-Moshinsky
          formula of Kamuntavicius et al. (2001), evaluated independently
          by tmb_kam.f90;
    (v)   the S(3) relations carried by the d = 1/3 brackets, where
          P23 = HOB(1/3) and P12 = diag((-1)^l1):
              P23^2 = I     and     (P12 P23)^3 = I.

  Note (ii) is necessary but NOT sufficient: it vanishes identically under a
  spurious orthogonal rotation of a block, so it bounds only the
  non-orthogonal part of the error.



bench/

  ladder    Emax     per-shell prepare / evaluate times and max |HOB.HOB^T - I|


  Representative single-core figures (gfortran -O2), from bench/ladder:

      E = 30   prepare 0.16 s   evaluate 0.14 s   max|HOB.HOB^T - I| 1.5e-10
      E = 50   prepare 5.9  s   evaluate 7.1  s   max|HOB.HOB^T - I| 1.8e-06

  The whole E <= 50 range is reachable; accuracy degrades smoothly.


ACCOMPANYING ARTICLE

  A. Stepsys, S. Mickevicius, D. Germanas, "SU3HOB: a Fortran package for
  harmonic-oscillator brackets in the SU(3) basis from pseudo-spin ladder
  operators".

  It describes the method, compares it against two independent routes to the
  same brackets, and applies it to three-particle coefficients of fractional
  parentage.  The article is not part of this source tree.  Every table in it
  can be reproduced with 'make bench'; the logs from the runs quoted there are
  in logs/, and the MANIFEST says which log backs which table.


FILES

  hob_su3.f90        the method: coupled basis, J+ construction, kernel +
                     lowering, Wigner d-functions, bracket assembly
  WignerSymbol.f90   SU(2) Clebsch-Gordan coefficients, used to build the
                     J+ matrix elements.  Bundled unmodified from the
                     WignerSymbol package,
                     https://github.com/0382/WignerSymbol,
                     Copyright (c) 2022 0382, MIT License
  tmb_kam.f90        the classical Talmi-Moshinsky bracket, from the compact
                     expression of Kamuntavicius et al., Nucl. Phys. A695
                     (2001) 191, Eq. (26).  The 6j (Sec. 9.2.1), 9j
                     (Sec. 10.2.4) and Clebsch-Gordan (Secs. 8.2.1, 8.5.1)
                     coefficients are those of Varshalovich, Moskalev and
                     Khersonskii.  Factorials and double factorials are
                     tabulated in logarithms rather than as binomial and
                     trinomial tables, which is what carries the expression
                     past E ~ 12 to E = 50.  Used only by the validation
                     driver; the library itself does not depend on it
  hob.f90            command-line front end
  test_hob_su3.f90   validation driver      test_hob_su3.ref  its reference
  bench/             timing and accuracy drivers (see above)
  logs/              measurement logs behind the tables of the article
  Makefile, LICENSE, MANIFEST, .gitignore


